summary='''# Mark 6 — readiness follow-up

Dan approved the **v3 music level**. The exact preview hash and reproducible level settings are saved in ../music-preview-v3/producer-level-approval.json. Keep this level; future final-cast mix checks compare against it rather than changing it by default. This does not imply final picture/placement/native/release or production-spend approval.

Read-only checks confirm all five named speaking canon versions, exact voice IDs, 16 image asset hashes and four approved audition output hashes. Thirteen concrete speaking briefs now pin source bounds, character/version/voice, existing references, full-line reuse, acting intent and framing/continuity checks. Four take hashes are reusable; nine other named lines remain unvoiced pending authorization.

The short-speaking planner now finds a complete measured-quiet route when a fixed balanced section count would cut during speech. For Jesus' Mark 6:4 source line this uses four sections rather than three. Every source sample remains consecutive; full-line audio is unchanged. If no route exists, uncertainty remains explicit. Three collective source lines still have quiet-free spans longer than four seconds; proposed listener/context pictures preserve their whole soundtrack without inventing a safe speech edit. Final approved cast bytes still require their own partition and AV review.

Updated source estimate: **44 named speaking containers + 85 coverage = 129 initial local video requests**; the proposed 160-request envelope and other draft budgets are unchanged. Speaking inference alone projects 10.00 hours at the historical median, not a whole-chapter ETA. The original full-on-camera alternative rises to 69 known speaking containers / 145 initial total, still excluding the held food reply.

The Mark 6:38 reply remains held for isolated revoicing/lip-sync; a continuous original-source/context treatment avoids making that uncertain cut, subject to normal crew casting/coverage decision. The named/source-brief preparation is complete; formal crew treatment, timed shots, group speakers, final frame crops and production budget authorization remain. No new Mark 6 workspace or paid call was made. Full production remains **ON HOLD**.
'''
(out/'README.md').write_text(summary,encoding='utf-8')
